# Decided
- "Needs a config guard" means a file whose #if/#ifdef/#ifndef/#elif
  reads a macro that include/sqlite_orm/sqlite_orm_config.h #defines
  (55 on dev). 83 files match; named_module.cpp already had the include,
  so 82 get it: 13 examples, 68 tests, prepared_common.h.
- Placement: directly after <sqlite_orm/sqlite_orm.h>, where sorted
  includes put it; no comment on the line.
- Inputs stay out: SQLITE_ORM_OMITS_CODECVT is public (#1591; on dev a
  CMake option, INTERFACE definition on target sqlite_orm), but the build
  defines it, the config header only reads it - like
  SQLITE_ORM_ENABLE_LOAD_EXTENSION. Hence simple_query.cpp and tests3.cpp
  (only OMITS_CODECVT / SERIES_*) are left alone.
- trueqbit: the commit body drops "today"; the include states the
  dependency for the named-module case, no breakage is fixed.

